+    static final Pattern MIXED_FENCE = Pattern.compile("(?m)^[^`~\\r\\n]*(`{3,}[^`\\r\\n]*~|~{3,}[^\\r\\n]*`)");
+    /**
+     * A thematic break of dashes only (a setext underline's shape) on the line right after a link reference
+     * definition: commonmark.js gives {@code "[foo]: /url\n---\n"} an empty paragraph before the {@code <hr />} (the
+     * definition-only paragraph the underline closes is emitted empty); the library, cmark and the spec (§Link
+     * reference definitions: a definition-only paragraph is no paragraph) give the {@code <hr />} alone. With
+     * {@code ***}, {@code ___} or {@code - - -} commonmark.js agrees.
